<style>
  /* Scoped to #tcf so the dark scene palette does not leak into other pages. */
  #tcf {
    --surface-1: #1a1a19;
    --page: #0d0d0d;
    --text-primary: #ffffff;
    --text-secondary: #c3c2b7;
    --text-muted: #898781;
    --hairline: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10);
    --gridline: #2c2c2a;
    --series-return: #3987e5;   /* categorical slot 1, dark step */
    --series-outflow: #d95926;  /* categorical slot 2, dark step */
    --series-reserve: #199e70;  /* categorical slot 3, dark step */
    --series-leak: #898781;     /* recessive: value lost from the loop */
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100vh;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--page);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  }
  #toroidal-cash-flow-container {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }
  #tcf .scene-label {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  }
  #tcf .scene-label small {
    display: block;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 10px;
  }
  #tcf #panel {
    position: absolute;
    top: 16px;
    left: 16px;
    width: 320px;
    max-height: calc(100vh - 32px);
    overflow-y: auto;
    background: rgba(26, 26, 25, 0.85);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 16px;
    z-index: 10;
  }
  #tcf #panel h1 {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  #tcf #panel p.sub {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  #tcf .legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 14px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  #tcf .legend span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  #tcf .legend i {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  #tcf .tiles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  #tcf .tile {
    background: var(--surface-1);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 8px 10px;
  }
  #tcf .tile .k {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  #tcf .tile .v {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 650;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  #tcf .tile .d {
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 1px;
  }
  #tcf #spark {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 26px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  #tcf .controls {
    margin-top: 14px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  #tcf .controls label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  #tcf .controls label b {
    float: right;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  #tcf .controls input[type="range"] {
    width: 100%;
    margin-top: 4px;
    accent-color: var(--series-return);
  }
  #tcf .note {
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding-top: 10px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>

<div id="tcf">
  <div id="toroidal-cash-flow-container"></div>

  <aside id="panel">
    <h1>Toroidal Cash Flow</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      A business as a closed flow.
      Money rises through the core, radiates out as spending, circles the outside, and returns as revenue.
      Reserves are the pause at the still point — not the opposite of flow, a phase of it.
    </p>

    <div class="legend">
      <span><i style="background: var(--series-outflow)"></i>Outflow</span>
      <span><i style="background: var(--series-return)"></i>Return</span>
      <span><i style="background: var(--series-reserve)"></i>Reserves</span>
      <span><i style="background: var(--series-leak)"></i>Leakage</span>
    </div>

    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="k">Reserves</div>
        <div
          class="v"
          id="t-reserve"
        >—</div>
        <canvas id="spark"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="k">Closure</div>
        <div
          class="v"
          id="t-closure"
        >—</div>
        <div class="d">measured, of passes</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="k">Cycle time</div>
        <div
          class="v"
          id="t-cycle"
        >—</div>
        <div class="d">avg loop, incl. dwell</div>
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <div class="k">Leaked</div>
        <div
          class="v"
          id="t-leaked"
        >—</div>
        <div class="d">cumulative</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="controls">
      <label>
        Closure — share of outflow that returns
        <b id="v-closure">85%</b>
        <input
          id="c-closure"
          type="range"
          min="0"
          max="100"
          value="85"
        >
      </label>
      <label>
        Velocity — speed of circulation
        <b id="v-speed">1.0×</b>
        <input
          id="c-speed"
          type="range"
          min="10"
          max="300"
          value="100"
        >
      </label>
      <label>
        Dwell — pause held in reserve at the core
        <b id="v-dwell">1.2s</b>
        <input
          id="c-dwell"
          type="range"
          min="0"
          max="400"
          value="120"
        >
      </label>
      <label>
        Rhythm — pulsed vs. steady flow
        <b id="v-rhythm">40%</b>
        <input
          id="c-rhythm"
          type="range"
          min="0"
          max="80"
          value="40"
        >
      </label>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      Each mote is ≈ $100 of working capital.
      Watch the reserve gauge: high closure with some dwell holds it steady; low closure drains the loop no matter how fast it spins.
      Velocity has a shape — the same speed can be a healthy torus or a fast leak.
      Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom.
      Companion to <em>geometric-finance.md</em> (tink).
    </p>
  </aside>
</div>

<script>
  window.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    window.toroidalCashFlow();
  });
</script>
